{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Crime and Punishment", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Trial Swap", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe rules and obligations through a wider range of language and expressions in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Be Supposed To ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the structure<span class=\"strong\"> be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the past, present or future.<br /><br />  The structure is:<br /><br />  Subject + To be + supposed to + verb<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">Twelve people <span class=\"strong\">are supposed to decide</span> whether the accused is guilty or innocent. </span><br /><br /><br />   **Pronunciation tip**:<br /> When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together. <br /><br />  Like this:<br /> Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Anthony was supposed to be in court for a petty crime.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Roy was supposed to be on trial for credit card fraud.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He was immediately taken to a maximum security prison and was supposed to face up to 15 years in prison.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Past Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about an action that was happening at a time before now. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Past Continuous to:<br /><br />  <ul> \t<li>to describe the background in a story written in the past tense </li> </ul> For example: <br /><span class=\"italic\">The children <span class=\"strong\">were laughing </span>and the birds <span class=\"strong\">were singing</span> in the park. A woman <span class=\"strong\">was looking </span>for her phone, which she dropped somewhere ...</span><br /><br />  <ul> \t<li>to describe an action that was interrupted by another event or action</li> </ul>  For example:<br /><span class=\"italic\"> I <span class=\"strong\">was reading </span>the news the other day <span class=\"strong\">when I came across </span>an article that talked about a trial by judge.</span><br /><br />  The form of the Past Continuous is:<br /><br />  Subject + was/were + verb-ing", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They met while they were waiting together in the holding cell on their way to their own separate trials at the county court house.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "While Roy was being called by the judge, Anthony took his place. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Each were thinking that the other was in less trouble than himself and decided to switch places for their court appearances.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to illustrate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to show", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The story of Roy Rivers and Anthony Jackson illustrates the expression \"justice works in mysterious ways.\"", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about crime and punishment.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "holding cell", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small room where people wait to have their trial", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They met while they were waiting together in the holding cell.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mistakenly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "by mistake", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Roy mistakenly thought that Anthony was supposed to be in court for a petty crime.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fraud", "type": "name"}, {"content": "criminal deception intended to result in financial gain", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Roy was supposed to be on trial for credit card fraud.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "court appearance ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the moment when a person faces a judge, jury or lawyer", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They decided to switch places for their court appearances.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "swap ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the condition of switching places", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Nobody noticed the swap.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "small-time", "type": "name"}, {"content": "minor", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Anthony was shocked to discover that Roy wasn't a small-time drug seller.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "smuggler", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who secretly transports illegal materials", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Roy was one of the biggest drug smugglers in the country.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob06aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be wanted ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be a target for police", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Anthony had been arrested for murder and was wanted in over 10 states.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob06aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to face ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look at your future ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He was immediately taken to a maximum security prison and was supposed to face up to 15 years in prison.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob06aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le03ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Yesterday a house was robbed between 4:00 p.m and 6:00 p.m. The police are asking the neighbors for information.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In your group of four, one student is the police officer and the other students are neighbors.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The police officer will ask the neighbors what they were doing yesterday between 4:00 and 6:00.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The neighbors will tell the police officer what they were doing. (Make up whatever you want!)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The police officer will decide who he thinks is a suspect in the robbery.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about rules, regulations, crime and punishment.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about what is supposed to happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about what I was doing or what is happening.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_o